\label{fig:class_diagram}
\end{figure}

The class diagram in Figure \ref{fig:class_diagram} shows the main classes in the system and their relationships:

\begin{itemize}
    \item \texttt{QKDSimulator}: Responsible for implementing the BB84 protocol and generating shared secret keys. Methods include \texttt{generate\_quantum\_keys()}, \texttt{simulate\_quantum\_transmission()}, and \texttt{detect\_eavesdropping()}.
    
    \item \texttt{QuantumEncryption}: Handles encryption and decryption of data using the quantum-generated keys. Key methods include \texttt{encrypt\_data()}, \texttt{decrypt\_data()}, and \texttt{derive\_key()}.
    
    \item \texttt{FraudDetectionAI}: Provides AI-powered fraud detection capabilities with multiple model types, including a neural network model. Methods include \texttt{analyze\_transaction()}, \texttt{extract\_features()}, and \texttt{determine\_risk\_factors()}.
    
    \item \texttt{SimpleNN}: Implements a 4-layer neural network using PyTorch for advanced fraud detection, with methods for model training, prediction, and feature processing.
    
    \item \texttt{RazorpayIntegration}: Manages communication with the Razorpay API for payment processing. Methods include \texttt{create\_order()}, \texttt{process\_payment()}, and \texttt{verify\_signature()}.
    
    \item \texttt{ApplicationController}: Coordinates the entire flow and manages user interaction, orchestrating the communication between all components.
\end{itemize}

