The sequence diagram in Figure \ref{fig:sequence_diagram} illustrates the chronological flow of interactions between components during a transaction:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item The user initiates a payment transaction through the application interface
    \item The Application Controller requests quantum key generation from the QKD Module
    \item The QKD Module simulates the BB84 protocol and returns a secure key
    \item Payment data is encrypted using the quantum-derived key
    \item The encrypted transaction is analyzed by the neural network fraud detection system
    \item If the transaction passes fraud checks, a Razorpay order is created
    \item The payment is processed through the Razorpay API
    \item The payment result is verified and decrypted using the quantum key
    \item The final transaction result is displayed to the user
\end{enumerate}

This sequence ensures end-to-end security of the transaction data while maintaining compatibility with existing payment infrastructure.

